{title: Nothing Makes Them Stumble}
{subtitle: Psalms 119:165}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm7] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I rejoice over your promise [Eb]like [Gm7]one who finds great [Eb]spoil
[Bb]I hate and [Eb]detest falsehood but I [Gm7]love You, [Fsus4]Lord [Eb]
[Bb]Seven times a day I praise you [Eb]for your righteous judgments
[Gm7]My soul keeps your testimonies [Eb]and I love them deeply
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Great peace belongs to those who [Eb]love your law
[Gm7]And nothing makes them [Eb]stumble
[Bb]I wait for your salvation and [Eb]I follow your commandments
[Gm7]Great peace belongs to those who [Eb]love your law
[F]And nothing makes them [Bb]stumble [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]I keep your precepts and [Eb]your testimonies
[Gm7]For all my ways lie [Eb]open before you
[Bb]My soul keeps your testimo[Eb]nies and I love them deeply
[Gm7]Great peace belongs to those who [Eb]love your law
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Great peace belongs to those who [Eb]love your law
[Gm7]And nothing makes them [Eb]stumble
[Bb]I wait for your salvation and [Eb]I follow your commandments
[Gm7]Great peace belongs to those who [Eb]love your law
[Fsus4]And nothing makes them [Bb]stumble
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
I hate and [Eb]detest falsehood but I [Gm]love you, [Fsus4]Lord [Eb]
[Bb]Seven times a day I praise [Eb]you for your righteous judg[Gm7]ments
My soul keeps your testimonies [Eb]and I love them deeply
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm7]Great peace belongs to those who [Eb]love your law
[Fsus4]And nothing makes them [Bb]stumble
{end_of_verse}

